soc: sunxi: cpu-comm: the register whitelist is the hwspinlock's

known_regs[] is copied from the vendor module and the comment says so -
"known_regs @ 0x16350 in cpu_comm_dev.ko" - but the last two entries do not
say what the module says. The vendor bytes at file offset 0x16398 read
0x03061024, 0x03061028, 0x03004000, 0x03004010; ours listed 0x03003000 and
0x03003010 and called them "Msgbox channel register". Both are wrong by one
hex digit, and the label is wrong too.

Which block is which is settled by the board's own device tree, not by a
guess: hy310-stock.dts has msgbox@3003000 (reg 0x3003000/0x3003400/0x3003800,
0x400 each) at line 1403 and hwspinlock@3004000 (reg 0x3004000 size 0x1000,
num-locks 32) at line 1650. So the vendor whitelists two words of the
hardware spinlock controller - which is the block cpu_comm really uses, over
getRegbySpinID()'s logical id + 8 - and not the msgbox at all.

What a reader of those two words got before, and gets now: before, they were
inside reg_to_iomem()'s 0x03003000..0x03003fff window, so comm_ReadRegWord()
would have returned msgbox bank 0 at +0x00 and +0x10 - registers below the
+0x20 RX enable where the vendor's own address arithmetic starts, i.e. two
words of the wrong block. Now they name the hwspinlock controller's status
words (+0x00 is SPINLOCK_SYSSTATUS_REG in the in-tree sun6i_hwspinlock
driver), for which reg_to_iomem() has no window: a call would take the
"reg 0x%08x not mapped" branch and return 0 instead of a foreign register.

Nothing on the HY310 changes. comm_ReadRegWord() and comm_WriteRegWord() are
the only consumers of the array (is_known_reg()), no ioctl and no debugfs
file reaches them, and their only callers in the whole tree pass 0x03061024
(cpu_comm_dev.c, the shared-memory adoption check) and getShareRegbyID()'s
0x03061024 / 0x03061028. Neither of the two changed words is asked for
anywhere. Access to the spinlocks themselves goes through the hwspinlock
framework (comm_InitHwSpinLock), not through this array.

Source: umbau/work/AP3o/REPORT.txt section 7 and umbau/re-apps/AP3o/REVIEW.md
(F1), with the block assignment from hy310-stock.dts. Follow-up to 0014;
0014, 0014a to 0014d stay byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff -ruN a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_hw.c
@@ -29,13 +29,18 @@ u32 hwlock_counters[HW_SPINLOCK_COUNT];
 /*
  * Known register addresses — the only registers io_accessor will touch.
  * From IDA: known_regs @ 0x16350 in cpu_comm_dev.ko
+ *
+ * The last two are the vendor array's own words, read out of the module
+ * bytes (AP3o section 7). They belong to hwspinlock@3004000, not to
+ * msgbox@3003000 - reg_to_iomem() has no window for them, so a call for one
+ * of them is refused there; nothing in this driver asks for one.
  */
 static const u32 known_regs[] = {
 	0x0306101c,	/* MIPS status — bit 0 set when out of reset */
 	0x03061024,	/* MIPS ShareReg14 — SharedMemAddr */
 	0x03061028,	/* MIPS ShareReg13 — SharedMemSize */
-	0x03003000,	/* Msgbox channel register */
-	0x03003010,	/* Msgbox channel register */
+	0x03004000,	/* hwspinlock@3004000 +0x00 - SYSSTATUS */
+	0x03004010,	/* hwspinlock@3004000 +0x10 - lock status word */
 };
 
 static void __iomem *mips_ctrl_base;	/* ioremap of 0x03061000 */
